Assignment name  : zigzag
Expected files   : zigzag.c
Allowed functions: write
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Write a program that takes a string and displays it by alternating the case of
each character based on its position.

- Characters at even indexes (0, 2, 4, ...) must be in uppercase if they are
  lowercase letters.
- Characters at odd indexes (1, 3, 5, ...) must be in lowercase if they are
  uppercase letters.
- Other characters (non-alphabetical) must remain unchanged.

The result must be followed by a newline.

If the number of arguments is not 1, the program displays only a newline.

Examples:

$> ./zigzag "hello world" | cat -e
HeLlO WoRlD$

$> ./zigzag "ZIGZAG" | cat -e
ZiGzAg$

$> ./zigzag "123abcABC" | cat -e
123AbCaBc$

$> ./zigzag | cat -e
$
